 also be looked over for technical content. It is hoped that\, via two or t
 hree iterations\, we will have a close to perfect set of résumés by Janu
 ary 6. These will be shown off to industry partners.</div>\n<div class="el
 ementToProof">Below are some tips and general advice that should be noted 
 before you begin to create your résumés — please read these carefully.
  These were provided by some of the hiring managers amongst the alums.</di
 v>\n<h4 class="elementToProof">Advice on small details</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use
  appropriate file naming conventions — the "Surname_Name_VersionX.docx
 ” file name convention is preferred.  For example: 'Mosses_Claire_Vers
 ion1.docx'&nbsp\;</li>\n<li>Ensure all links to e-mail addresses/personal 
 pages are clickable.  If you are linking to a personal webpage/Linkedin 
 profile/GitHub repo also ensure that it is up-to-date.</li>\n<li>Ensure 
 that all the information (even the small information) detailed in your
  résumé is specific and accurately formatted\, for example\, 'mysql' s
 hould be 'MySQL'</li>\n<li>Keep the résumé to one page.</li>\n<li>Use bu
 llet points.</li>\n<li>Use correct spelling\, punctuation and grammar.</li
 >\n</ul>\n<h4 class="elementToProof">General advice on content</h4>\n<ul>\
 n<li>Order your sections appropriately\, and use the appropriate sections 
 (note the annotation of optional beside certain sections of the template).
  You don't have to use them all.</li>\n<li>Include the names of important 
 courses. Industry partners are interested in the graduate training you hav
 e\, but you may also have additional relevant training from other degrees.
  UofT course numbers often don't mean anything to people external to the U
 ofT.</li>\n<li>Ensure that the most impressive items are close to the top.
  For example\, if you have a lot of work experience\, the sections you use
  may be: Experience/Education/Skills/Awards.  If you have little/no wo
 rk experience you may have Skills/Education/Other Experience/Awards.&nbsp\
 ;You do not have to use all sections on the template.</li>\n<li>Get creati
 ve — have a play around with font/colour schemes and design — a few r
 ésumés last year were created in LaTeX\, which looked very professional.
 </li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Final tips</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Try and avoid using commas in
 stead of the word "and" — even if it saves space\, this isn't correct.</
 li>\n<li><span style="font-family: inherit\; font-size: 1rem\;">If you're 
 going to use links to github pages make sure they have substantial content
  on them. You don't have to include them\, so if whatever is behind the 
 links is largely inactive\, then you can take them out.</span> &nbsp\;</
