CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:This assignment has two components:\n\n1) Individual Presentati
 on Upload\n\n2) Peer review of presentations\n\nIndividual Presentation Up
 load\n------------------------------\n\nPrepare a 5-10 minute presentation
  on your project individually (or an alternative topic you may need to cov
 er at work or in interviews) and upload it. You can upload the presentatio
 n to YouTube or another platform and share the link on the discussion boar
 d. Make sure it is accessible to others. \n\nPlease keep the following in
  mind in your submission:\n\n* Please note that the submission deadline is
  November 28th\, so you can start early and upload your presentation by th
 is date.\n\n* You should not publicly list your presentation. It must be a
 vailable only with a link.\n\n* You are encouraged to do practice runs fir
 st and improve your presentation before you upload the final version. You 
 can practice in front of an audience and get their feedback\, as we have b
 een doing over the past several classes. \n\n* Your presentation must be 
 geared toward your classmates (unless you have a specific audience) who ha
 ve the technical foundations but don't know much about your project (comin
 g from other sections). Your goal is to inform them of what you have done 
 in your project. You can adjust the content as you wish.\n\n* You can use 
 the discussion board to ask questions.\n\nPeer Review\n-----------\n\nWe a
 ssign each of you two of your classmates from another section. Each of you
  will review the other person's presentation and critique it based on the 
 materials we have discussed. Each of you will be assigned 2 peer reviewer
 s. They will review your presentation and provide feedback based on the ma
 terial covered in class. You will leave your review and feedback on your p
 eers' presentations on Quercus by the last day of classes.\n\nYou must com
 plete both parts of this assignment to finish this module. You are encoura
 ged to iterate on your presentation based on your peer reviews\, but it is
  not required for the assignment.\n\n \n\nPlease note that this is sepa
 rate from the team presentations scheduled for your last cohort\, which yo
 u will present as a team live to the rest of your class and Karthik and Da
 vid. More details on this to come later. 
SEQUENCE:0
